  "question": {
    "text": "Two masses <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are connected by a string of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi></math>. They are held in a horizontal plane at a height&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>H</mi></math>&nbsp;above two heavy plates&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> made of different materials placed on the floor. Initially, the distance between the two masses is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>l</mi></math>. When the masses are released they fall freely and collide with the plates simultaneously. The coefficient of restitution for the collision of the first ball-plate pair is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn></math>&nbsp;and for the second ball-plate pair is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></math>. The time after the collision when the string becomes taut is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0013413_que.JPG\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 130px;\" />",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "mUNth",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi><mi>H</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>",
      "image": null,
